index 1c14edf4b..a182016a8 100644
--- a/docs/plugins/hooks/prompt-and-session.md
+++ b/docs/plugins/hooks/prompt-and-session.md
@@ -259,6 +259,21 @@ installs or updates. Do not publish a package that uses this option while
 claiming compatibility with an older plugin API; an older host may otherwise
 treat an unknown option as an ordinary pre-policy hook.
 
+Use `before_turn_start` to complete a required check before the Gateway
+dispatches a turn to the embedded harness, a Codex app server, or a paired
+worker. The event contains only `sessionId` and `runId`. OpenClaw resolves
+these IDs after the turn leaves the queue. A retry that enters the queue
+again can have the same IDs.
+
+Return from the handler to allow dispatch. A thrown error or a timeout stops
+dispatch and model fallback. The default timeout is 15 seconds. To require
+a specific plugin, set `OPENCLAW_REQUIRED_TURN_ADMISSION_PLUGIN` to its ID
+in the Gateway service environment. Each dispatch requires a successful call
+to that plugin, including after a plugin reload. The hook covers dispatch
+through session placement, including direct CLI turns. Commands that return
+before dispatch and individual model requests within a turn are outside
+this check.
+
 On the embedded and CLI runners, `before_agent_run` runs after prompt
 construction and before model submission, including `llm_input` observation.
 It receives the current user input as `prompt`, loaded session history in
